Article 985 of the Civil Code stipulates that where a beneficiary acquires unjust enrichment without legal basis, the person suffering loss may request the beneficiary to return the unjustly obtained benefits, except in the following cases:  
(1) Payments made to fulfill moral obligations;  
(2) Pre-expiration debt settlements;  
(3) Debt settlements made knowingly without obligation.  

